[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186138410 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cfe388a1-fc00-503a-b10d-218d6be786a1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cfe388a1-fc00-503a-b10d-218d6be786a1" :question/id #uuid "cfe388a1-fc00-503a-b10d-218d6be786a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-44531" :question/problem "Factor $3{n}^{5}+17{n}^{4}-28{n}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that all of the terms have a common factor of ${n}^{3}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${n}^{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{n}^{5}+17{n}^{4}-28{n}^{3} & ={n}^{3}(3{n}^{2}+17n-28)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the polynomial $3{n}^{2}+17n-28,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{3}(3{n}^{2}+17n-28) & = \\\\ {n}^{3}((3{n}^{2}-4n)+(21n-28)) & = \\\\ {n}^{3}((3n-4)n+(3n-4)7) & = \\\\ {n}^{3}(3n-4)(n+7)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-60e37793-57d8-5148-aa95-28701d621f67"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-60e37793-57d8-5148-aa95-28701d621f67" :answer-field/id #uuid "60e37793-57d8-5148-aa95-28701d621f67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a2f6c753-5968-5e31-b594-ba31ba82d2aa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4eae722a-276d-56a3-8d3f-0f4ca15c0011" "answer-c7f338ee-1cf8-53b5-9adf-f59a8579be4d" "answer-12e23d40-d227-5424-b5b7-586c63816d72" "answer-a2f6c753-5968-5e31-b594-ba31ba82d2aa" "answer-2fd4fa4b-4269-5a19-9696-33db33bf7069"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4eae722a-276d-56a3-8d3f-0f4ca15c0011" :answer/id #uuid "4eae722a-276d-56a3-8d3f-0f4ca15c0011" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{n}^{2}(2{n}^{2}-14)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7f338ee-1cf8-53b5-9adf-f59a8579be4d" :answer/id #uuid "c7f338ee-1cf8-53b5-9adf-f59a8579be4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{n}^{2}(n-4)(3n+7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12e23d40-d227-5424-b5b7-586c63816d72" :answer/id #uuid "12e23d40-d227-5424-b5b7-586c63816d72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{n}^{3}(3n+4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2f6c753-5968-5e31-b594-ba31ba82d2aa" :answer/id #uuid "a2f6c753-5968-5e31-b594-ba31ba82d2aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{n}^{3}(3n-4)(n+7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fd4fa4b-4269-5a19-9696-33db33bf7069" :answer/id #uuid "2fd4fa4b-4269-5a19-9696-33db33bf7069" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{n}^{3}(3n-7)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138409 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7cf33662-4ad6-5aa7-8431-3b990d895f49" "question-2c4e4328-a65d-5ebb-a442-4282ed74de70"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7cf33662-4ad6-5aa7-8431-3b990d895f49" :question/id #uuid "7cf33662-4ad6-5aa7-8431-3b990d895f49" :question/math-academy-id "q-69844" :question/problem "Factor the expression ${s}^{6}-4{s}^{5}+4{s}^{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of ${s}^{4}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${s}^{4},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{6}-4{s}^{5}+4{s}^{4} & ={s}^{4}({s}^{2}-4s+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression ${s}^{2}-4s+4$ is a perfect square trinomial that can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{4}({s}^{2}-4s+4) & = \\\\ {s}^{4}({s}^{2}-4s+{2}^{2}) & = \\\\ {s}^{4}({s}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot s+{2}^{2}) & = \\\\ {s}^{4}(s-2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-97ab82ae-a070-54e1-a8a1-4a953ee8477c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-97ab82ae-a070-54e1-a8a1-4a953ee8477c" :answer-field/id #uuid "97ab82ae-a070-54e1-a8a1-4a953ee8477c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6c382d23-03d9-5fba-94e6-efeccbf637e5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be84eb82-1c77-5ed7-8435-bb77d4b7d622" "answer-fe095cce-7414-588e-8038-6dedc80d8543" "answer-2e10bf21-a085-5225-9e50-b8399bd50bc9" "answer-6c382d23-03d9-5fba-94e6-efeccbf637e5" "answer-96a29d2f-4d5d-549b-80ab-68c608300205"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be84eb82-1c77-5ed7-8435-bb77d4b7d622" :answer/id #uuid "be84eb82-1c77-5ed7-8435-bb77d4b7d622" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}^{2}(s+2)^{2}(s-2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe095cce-7414-588e-8038-6dedc80d8543" :answer/id #uuid "fe095cce-7414-588e-8038-6dedc80d8543" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}^{3}(s-2)^{2}(s+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e10bf21-a085-5225-9e50-b8399bd50bc9" :answer/id #uuid "2e10bf21-a085-5225-9e50-b8399bd50bc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}^{4}(s+2)(s-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c382d23-03d9-5fba-94e6-efeccbf637e5" :answer/id #uuid "6c382d23-03d9-5fba-94e6-efeccbf637e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}^{4}(s-2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96a29d2f-4d5d-549b-80ab-68c608300205" :answer/id #uuid "96a29d2f-4d5d-549b-80ab-68c608300205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}^{5}(s-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2c4e4328-a65d-5ebb-a442-4282ed74de70" :question/id #uuid "2c4e4328-a65d-5ebb-a442-4282ed74de70" :question/math-academy-id "q-111940" :question/problem "Factor the expression ${h}^{7}+8{h}^{6}+16{h}^{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of ${h}^{5}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${h}^{5},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{7}+8{h}^{6}+16{h}^{5} & ={h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression ${h}^{2}+8h+16$ is a perfect square trinomial that can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+16) & = \\\\ {h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+{4}^{2}) & = \\\\ {h}^{5}({h}^{2}+2\\cdot 4h+{4}^{2}) & = \\\\ {h}^{5}(h+4)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f9a21e5e-fd27-5130-9714-620502136f1b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f9a21e5e-fd27-5130-9714-620502136f1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a21e5e-fd27-5130-9714-620502136f1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ee148d99-14db-571f-b95d-3fd724833b22" :answer-field/choices ["answer-040ec5ab-bcdf-5aca-99d8-720e6b5d8392" "answer-5d268b5c-01f0-51e5-95fd-adf189f6f7e5" "answer-574ae8f2-ab3d-5f65-a5ac-bc1418674da6" "answer-ee148d99-14db-571f-b95d-3fd724833b22" "answer-95c2c16a-d3fe-5fc6-bead-e655541975ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-040ec5ab-bcdf-5aca-99d8-720e6b5d8392" :answer/id #uuid "040ec5ab-bcdf-5aca-99d8-720e6b5d8392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h(h+4)^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d268b5c-01f0-51e5-95fd-adf189f6f7e5" :answer/id #uuid "5d268b5c-01f0-51e5-95fd-adf189f6f7e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{h}^{4}(h+4)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-574ae8f2-ab3d-5f65-a5ac-bc1418674da6" :answer/id #uuid "574ae8f2-ab3d-5f65-a5ac-bc1418674da6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{h}^{4}(h-4)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee148d99-14db-571f-b95d-3fd724833b22" :answer/id #uuid "ee148d99-14db-571f-b95d-3fd724833b22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{h}^{5}(h+4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95c2c16a-d3fe-5fc6-bead-e655541975ee" :answer/id #uuid "95c2c16a-d3fe-5fc6-bead-e655541975ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{h}^{5}(h-4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-132a1609-d838-5cdf-86ad-3b381309c84b" :activity/id #uuid "132a1609-d838-5cdf-86ad-3b381309c84b" :activity/title "Further Factoring of Polynomials Using GCFs"