49" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-97ab82ae-a070-54e1-a8a1-4a953ee8477c"] [17592186138409 :knowledge-point/questions "question-7cf33662-4ad6-5aa7-8431-3b990d895f49"] ["question-2c4e4328-a65d-5ebb-a442-4282ed74de70" :question/id #uuid "2c4e4328-a65d-5ebb-a442-4282ed74de70"] ["question-2c4e4328-a65d-5ebb-a442-4282ed74de70" :question/math-academy-id "q-111940"] ["question-2c4e4328-a65d-5ebb-a442-4282ed74de70" :question/problem "Factor the expression ${h}^{7}+8{h}^{6}+16{h}^{5}.$"] ["question-2c4e4328-a65d-5ebb-a442-4282ed74de70" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of ${h}^{5}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${h}^{5},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{7}+8{h}^{6}+16{h}^{5} & ={h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression ${h}^{2}+8h+16$ is a perfect square trinomial that can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+16) & = \\\\ {h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+{4}^{2}) & = \\\\ {h}^{5}({h}^{2}+2\\cdot 4h+{4}^{2}) & = \\\\ {h}^{5}(h+4)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-2c4e4328-a65d-5ebb-a442-4282ed74de70" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-f9a21e5e-fd27-5130-9714-620502136f1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a21e5e-fd27-5130-9714-620502136f1b"] ["answer-040ec5ab-bcdf-5aca-99d8-720e6b5d8392" :answer/id #uuid "040ec5ab-bcdf-5aca-99d8-720e6b5d8392"] ["answer-040ec5ab-bcdf-5aca-99d8-720e6b5d8392" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-040ec5ab-bcdf-5aca-99d8-720e6b5d8392" :answer/value "h(h+4)^{6}"] ["answer-5d268b5c-01f0-51e5-95fd-adf189f6f7e5" :answer/id #uuid "5d268b5c-01f0-51e5-95fd-adf189f6f7e5"] ["answer-5d268b5c-01f0-51e5-95fd-adf189f6f7e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5d268b5c-01f0-51e5-95fd-adf189f6f7e5" :answer/value "{h}^{4}(h+4)^{3}"] ["answer-574ae8f2-ab3d-5f65-a5ac-bc1418674da6" :answer/id #uuid "574ae8f2-ab3d-5f65-a5ac-bc1418674da6"] ["answer-574ae8f2-ab3d-5f65-a5ac-bc1418674da6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answ